# Star Trek Galaxies -- sprites for the Trek event pictures our story events use.
#
# A THIRD new file beside interface/stg_event_pictures.gfx and
# interface/stg_arcsite_pictures.gfx, for the reason the second one exists: the
# three databases are read by three different checks, and a session that breaks
# one should not have to read the other two. Everything in the first file's
# header applies here unchanged:
#
#   TWO SPRITES PER PICTURE -- interface/eventpictures.gfx says "the Situation
#   Log automatically uses sprites with the _nomask suffix if available".
#
#   The art is 620x264 or a 9315x264 animation strip in .source/; `target:
#   family` on gfx/event_pictures in vendor.yml re-cuts it to vanilla's 450x150
#   at harvest, freezing frame 0 of a strip. Without that this file is decision
#   42's defect: UIOD's eventwindow.gui draws at scale = 1.5 inside a 693x239
#   frame, so 620x264 art renders 930x396.
#   See .docs/decisions/69-event-picture-families.md.
#
# ALL 21 WERE LOOKED AT AS THE BUILD WILL CUT THEM -- frame 0, centre-cropped to
# 450x150 -- and eight candidates were rejected on what that crop showed: two
# Lower-Decks-animated frames, three close-ups of a named character's face, one
# near-featureless star field (bajoranWormhole1, whose wormhole has not opened
# yet in frame 0) and two that read as a different subject than the filename
# promised. Same standard as .docs/decisions/70-trek-anomalies.md set.
#
# THREE CANDIDATES WERE DROPPED FOR THE OPPOSITE REASON -- engineering_bay,
# cargoship_caravan and galactic_market are STNH shipping VANILLA'S OWN picture
# under vanilla's own name, so they are neither Trek nor ours to declare. The
# filter is one line: 580 of STNH's 1,350 names also exist in
# /stellaris/gfx/event_pictures, and only the other 770 are art STNH added.
#
# NONE OF THE 21 IS DECLARED BY EITHER SIBLING. One picture, one subject.
#
# See .docs/decisions/72-trek-story-events.md

spriteTypes = {

	# ── The twelve peoples' own institutions ─────────────────────────────────
	spriteType = {
		name = "GFX_evt_stg_academy_class"
		texturefile = "gfx/event_pictures/starfleet_academy.dds"
